sysctl -a | grep -i "sched" will show parameters that are modifiable at runtime under /proc/sys

cat /proc/sched_stat will show some useless information see show_schedstat for formatting.

cat /proc/sched_debug will list out useful information including whats on the runqueue ( or the tree that they use ). 
This is useful.

cat /proc/pid/sched  | grep -i "nr_switches" will provide information about voluntary/ involuntary switches


taskset -p 0x2 pid will make sure pid only runs on process 1 (its a bit mask)

chrt will allow you to dynamically change scheduling class

renice will do what you think it will :-)